$( -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Stage 4: relation-algebra reduction of the first-pivot graph
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------

   Let S be the homogeneous separator relation, and let R^si be the singleton
   lift of the displayed well-order R.  The graph Q required by
   fdpivmapexlem is

       Q = S \\ ( S o. (R^si)^-1 ).

   Membership in the composition says exactly that an earlier separator
   exists.  Thus the previous one-shot Hailperin construction is reduced to
   sethood of the typed incidence relations used to form S.  The intended
   construction of S is the symmetric difference of the two incidence
   relations obtained by composing typed membership with the two homogeneous
   projections from the point-pair code.

   No new theorem is asserted in this worksheet block.  The exact interfaces
   and proof order are recorded in nf_wpp_pivot_factorization.md and
   nf_wpp_separator_algebra.md. $)

$( Self-contained copy of the verified well-order extraction and strict-minimality bridge. $)

