$( A set-coded precursor to the typed Lindenbaum construction.

   LNTP is the class of reflexive, transitive, connected relation/base
   pairs: total preorders, without yet imposing well-foundedness.

   LNTPC A restricts these to normalized relations whose support is exactly
   A.  HWRels supplies the normalization R C_ ( A X. A ); the product with
   { A } fixes the represented base.

   LNKer R is the symmetric kernel R i^i `' R.  LNQuo ( R , A ) is the
   corresponding quotient carrier A /. LNKer R.  For a genuine
   prewellordering this carrier is the ordinal onto which A maps.  The
   induced quotient order and its well-foundedness are deliberately left as
   the next obligation; no Lindenbaum-number claim is made here. $)

$c LNTP LNTPC LNKer LNQuo $.

clntp $a class LNTP $.
clntpc $a class LNTPC A $.
clnker $a class LNKer R $.
clnquo $a class LNQuo ( R , A ) $.

${
  $d c e R A $.
df-lntp $a |- LNTP = ( ( Ref i^i Trans ) i^i Connex ) $.
$}

${
  $d c e R A $.
df-lntpc $a |- LNTPC A =
  ( ( LNTP i^i HWRels ) i^i ( _V X. { A } ) ) $.
$}

${
  $d c e R A $.
df-lnker $a |- LNKer R = ( R i^i `' R ) $.
$}

${
  $d c e R A $.
df-lnquo $a |- LNQuo ( R , A ) = ( A /. LNKer R ) $.
$}

