$( Phase-four audit body from lindenbaum_global_final.mm. $)
$( A global, type-correct envelope for the well-order types obtained by
   quotienting normalized prewellorders.  A quotient carrier consists of
   subsets of the original carrier, so the natural fixed ambient base is
   `~P A`, not `A` itself.

   `LNWCode ( R , D )` packages the quotient order and quotient carrier.
   `LNWCodes A` is the set of normalized well-order codes over the raised
   ambient base.  `LNWIso A` is the already explicit, generated
   isomorphism relation on those codes, and `LNWTypes A` is its quotient.
   Subsequent theorems prove that every member of `LNPWC A` contributes its
   quotient code and hence its isomorphism type to this set-coded envelope. $)

$c LNWCode LNWCodes LNWIso LNWTypes $.

clnwcode $a class LNWCode ( R , D ) $.
clnwcodes $a class LNWCodes A $.
clnwiso $a class LNWIso A $.
clnwtypes $a class LNWTypes A $.

${
  $d c e R A $.
df-lnwcode $a |- LNWCode ( R , D ) =
  <. LNQOrd ( R , D ) , LNQuo ( R , D ) >. $.
$}

${
